DESIGN ELEMENTS:
This overlay diagram illustrates the introduction of
windbreak shelterbelts that provide an organizing
element to the site.  They provide a level of comfort
and wind protection from the prevailing winds from the
northwest and extend the capacity of the adjacent HPA
to provide a variety of tree and understory species
for learning and interpretation as well as resource
protection.  As a design element, the plantings also
provide a visual and physical connection to the historic
arboretum plantings of the adjacent HPA.
Below the windbreak shelterbelt is the ‘Serenity Trail’,
a planted trail system that  loops through the cemetery
arboretum and introduces connections to the HPA.
The plant massings frame open space and vistas
across the existing landscape of the High Plains.
SUMMARY OF ORGANIZING DESIGN ELEMENTS:
•
Shelterbelt windbreaks for site organization,
interpretation and resource protection
•
Looped trail system within the windbreak
shelterbelt
•
Connectivity to the High Plains Arboretum
