SUMMARY OF ORGANIZING DESIGN ELEMENTS:
•
Flexible road network and consideration for future
expansion
•
Serenity value of a continuous and sweeping road
network
•
Centralized facilities for visitor contact and
orientation
DESIGN ELEMENTS:
This overlay diagram illustrates the continuous road
network through the cemetery arboretum.  The
alignment from the north on Hildreth Road allows for
a phased introduction of cemetery arboretum event
parking and short term parking for the visitor contact
facilities.  Facilities are centrally located for initial
visitor contact and orientation. The plan also allows
for centralized parking expansion into the previously
planned HPA site development area.
The road system within the cemetery arboretum
is continuous with monumented intersections for
vehicular wayﬁ nding.  The introduction of curved road
sections connects visitors with the natural topography
of a high plains landscape and reinforces the sweeping
nature of the shelterbelt plantings.  The motorists
views within the cemetery arboretum becomes a
guided experience of vistas and focal points that adds
serenity value to the visitor experience.
As the cemetery expands in future design phases to
the south and east, the major collector road provides
an organizing element along which future loop roads
and shelterbelts can be easily added.
