DESIGN ELEMENTS:
This overlay diagram illustrates the pedestrian
corridors for navigation and wayﬁ nding  through
the cemetery arboretum for visiting interred family
members.  Within the naturally sweeping landscape
and road system the gridded plot and pedestrian
circulation system provides a logical method of
navigating the cemetery.  On street parking provides
initial proximity to the sections and rows identiﬁ ed by
pedestrian scaled markers at the road interface.
For committal ceremonies the shared committal
shelters are co-located with the re-purposed ofﬁ ce
and greenhouse buildings and include close in ADA
parking as well as drop off lanes for hearst and family
precession vehicles.
The National Burial Grounds includes self contained
parking and can also be accessed on foot along the
east-west corridor that threads through loops A, B and
C or via the western trail that extends southward from
the committal shelters.
